/* ===== RELIGIOUS STUDIES · SINHALA (faith pack, July 2026) =====
   PRIMARILY FOR SINHALA PEOPLE (Sri Lanka) to learn about Jesus — Sinhala is
   the primary language everywhere (titles, story text, explanations), with
   English the quiet second line. Mirrors faith/ne.js: the same two stories,
   the same 10+10 big-moment sections, the same shared scene art.
   Deliberately Christian (the secular-content rule does NOT apply in faith
   mode). Content register: rich storytelling for the un-churched reader —
   every person, place and church-word introduced in-story on first use
   (Adam & Eve, Eden, Noah, Abraham, sacrifice, the prophets, exile,
   disciples, Mary Magdalene). Paraphrase only — no Bible-translation text is
   copied; references name the passages retold.
   REGISTER DECISION — spoken, not literary. Sinhala is strongly diglossic,
   and the Sinhala Bible is written in the LITERARY register with honorific
   verb endings (John 3:16: ...ප්‍රේම කළ සේක්... දෙවා වදාළ සේක්). This pack
   deliberately uses SPOKEN Sinhala instead, because (a) the course itself
   teaches spoken Sinhala — see lang/si.js — so the two stay consistent, and
   (b) the audience is an un-churched reader, for whom liturgical Sinhala is
   a second barrier on top of a new story. Respect is carried the way spoken
   Sinhala carries it: by the honorific NOUNS දෙවියන් වහන්සේ and යේසුස්
   වහන්සේ, which Sinhala Christians use in ordinary speech, with ordinary
   spoken verb forms (කළා, දුන්නා) rather than කළ සේක් / වදාළ සේක්.
   Vocabulary: දෙවියන් වහන්සේ (God), යේසුස් වහන්සේ (Jesus), ස්වාමීන් වහන්සේ
   (Lord), පුතා / පුත්‍රයා (Son), පාපය (sin), විශ්වාස කරනවා / විශ්වාසය
   (believe / faith), ආදරය (love), ගළවනවා / ගැළවීම (save / salvation),
   ගැළවුම්කරු (Rescuer), ශුභාරංචිය (gospel), කුරුසිය (cross), ශුද්ධාත්මයාණන්
   වහන්සේ (Holy Spirit), පොරොන්දුව (promise), ගිවිසුම (covenant),
   අනාගතවක්තෘවරයා (prophet), ගෝලයා (disciple), පූජාව (sacrifice),
   පිටුවහල් කිරීම (exile), රාජ්‍යය (kingdom), ස්වර්ගය (heaven),
   දේවමාළිගාව (temple), බව්තීස්මය (baptism), යාච්ඤා කරනවා (pray),
   දේවදූතයා (angel), බැටළු පැටවා (lamb), උත්ථානය (resurrection),
   සදාකාල ජීවනය (eternal life).
   Romanization follows the Sinhala course scheme in lang/si.js (ASCII;
   dental t/d written th/dh, retroflex plain t/d; ව=w, ච=ch, ශ/ෂ=sh, ං=ng;
   doubled vowels are held longer). Sinhala uses WESTERN NUMERALS, so this
   pack carries no digits[] array (same as mn). Native strings must avoid the
   chars ' " < > \ (they ride inline onclick handlers).
   IMPORTANT: keep paras[i][0] AND note[0] byte-stable once audio exists —
   clips in audio-sif/ are hashed from these exact strings. Regenerate with
     osascript -l JavaScript extract_audio_strings.js sif
     python3 generate_audio.py --lang sif
   Scene art is shared with the Nepali pack (language-independent scene
   emblems — scenes and symbols only, no depictions of God or of Jesus'
   face). */
